add(76,
'The bar chart compares the proportion of renewable energy in the total energy supply of Australia, Sweden, Iceland and Turkey in 1997, 2000 and 2010.',
'Overall, there was an increase in the renewable-energy shares of Iceland and Sweden, while Australia and Turkey ended below their initial levels. In addition, Iceland consistently had the highest figures and recorded the largest rise.',
'In Iceland, renewable sources supplied approximately 45% of energy in 1997. This figure increased to 60% in 2000 and 70% in 2010, widening its lead over the other countries. Turkey had the second highest figures, starting at around 38%. Its share rose to about 40% in 2000 but then fell to approximately 32% by the end of the period.',
'The proportions in Australia and Sweden were much smaller, remaining below 10% throughout. Australia’s share fell from roughly 9% in 1997 to 7% in 2000 and 5% in 2010. Sweden showed the opposite overall pattern, increasing from around 6% to 7% and then 9%. Thus, Australia began slightly above Sweden, but their positions were reversed in the final year.',
'Đơn vị % nguồn cung năng lượng; Iceland cao nhất, Australia giảm. Các cột nhỏ được đọc xấp xỉ.',
'Body 1: Iceland–Turkey. Body 2: Australia–Sweden.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','compare'])
hold(77,'Lời đề ghi Australia 1980/1990/2000 nhưng pie thứ ba ghi SWEDEN thay vì 2000. Cần xác nhận nhãn trước khi bắt học bài mẫu.')
hold(78,'Lời đề ghi proportion nhưng hai trục ghi % US…/nhãn không đầy đủ, các vạch và nhãn trục lệch nhau. Cần xác nhận giá trị/đơn vị trước khi chốt full bài; không tự chọn nhãn hay vạch.')
hold(79,'Lời đề 1911–2001 không khớp cột 1991/1961/2011; nhãn Total Population (Millions) không khớp định dạng số. Cần nguồn sửa trước khi mô tả.')
hold(80,'Biểu đồ chi nghiên cứu không có đơn vị tiền/trục tung. Không tự giả định billion dollars dù đó có thể là bản đề quen thuộc.')
hold(81,'Ảnh thiếu câu hỏi và các nhãn năm 2006/2008 bị lệch dưới trục; chưa xác định chắc ánh xạ năm–điểm. Cần bản rõ hơn trước khi soạn mẫu cố định.')
hold(82,'Hai biểu đồ độ tuổi kết hôn thiếu đơn vị trục tung. Chưa rõ là tỷ lệ, số người hay số nghìn; cần xác nhận trước khi dùng số trong bài mẫu.')
add(83,
'The pie charts compare the main forms of transport used by people travelling to a university in 2004 and 2009.',
'Overall, there was a decline in the proportion of students travelling by car, while a rise was seen in all four other modes of transport. In addition, buses replaced cars as the most common choice in 2009, although their share remained below half.',
'In 2004, cars were used by 51% of people travelling to the university, making this the only category with more than half of the total. Buses were the second most popular option, at 33%. Bicycles accounted for 9%, while walking and train travel were much less common, with shares of 4% and 3% respectively.',
'By 2009, the proportion using cars had fallen by 23 percentage points to 28%. In contrast, bus use rose to 46%, putting it well ahead of every other option. Cycling also became more common, increasing from 9% to 16%. The changes in the two smallest categories were more modest: walking rose to 6% and train travel to 4%. Together, these two forms still represented only one tenth of journeys in the final year.',
'Bus 46% là nhóm lớn nhất, không phải majority. Car 51% năm 2004 mới là majority; train3→4 và walking4→6.',
'Body 1: cơ cấu 2004. Body 2: thay đổi 2009.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','respectively'],{'years':[2004,2009],'unit':'percent','car':[51,28],'bicycle':[9,16],'bus':[33,46],'train':[3,4],'walking':[4,6]})
add(84,
'The bar chart compares the number of films produced in five countries, labelled A to E, in 2007, 2008 and 2009.',
'Overall, there was an increase in film production in Countries B, C and E, while Country A declined at the end and Country D fluctuated. In addition, Country A consistently had the highest figures, followed by Country B.',
'Country A made approximately 85 films in both 2007 and 2008, before its output fell to around 78 in 2009. Country B followed a different pattern, producing just under 50 films in 2007 and about 50 in 2008. Its figure then rose sharply to roughly 68 in the final year, narrowing the gap with Country A.',
'The remaining three countries produced far fewer films. Country C increased from around 7 films in 2007 to 12 in 2008 and 15 in 2009, more than doubling its output. Country D began at approximately 14, fell to about 9 and then recovered to around 12. Country E showed the smallest changes, rising from roughly 9 to 10 and then 11 films, while remaining close to the bottom of the group.',
'A cao nhất, B thứ hai; C tăng từ nền thấp. Các giá trị không in số nên dùng approximately/about.',
'Body 1: A/B lớn. Body 2: C/D/E nhỏ.',['intro','overview-trend','sequence','from-to'])
add(85,
'The bar chart compares the percentage of government spending devoted to roads and transport in Italy, Portugal, the UK and the USA in 1990, 1995, 2000 and 2005.',
'Overall, there was a decline in the proportion of government spending on roads and transport in Italy, Portugal and the UK, while a rise was seen in the USA. In addition, Portugal generally had the highest figures, although Italy overtook it in 2000, while the UK consistently recorded the lowest proportions.',
'Portugal’s share fell from approximately 27% in 1990 to 24% in 1995 and 22% in 2000, before ending at 20%. Italy started at around 22%, then dropped to 20% in 1995. Its figure recovered to about 24% in 2000, briefly overtaking Portugal, but declined again to roughly 19% in the final year.',
'The UK devoted a much smaller proportion to roads and transport, beginning at around 10%. This fell slightly in 1995, rose to approximately 12% in 2000 and then dropped to about 8% in 2005. The USA started at roughly 11% and also experienced a small initial fall. However, its share subsequently increased to around 14% in 2000 and 15% in 2005, closing some of the gap with Italy and Portugal.',
'Portugal generally, không consistently cao nhất vì Italy vượt năm 2000. Dữ liệu là share ngân sách, không phải tiền tuyệt đối.',
'Body 1: Portugal–Italy cao. Body 2: UK–USA thấp.',['intro','overview-trend','sequence','from-to'])
add(86,
'The table compares several population measures for Australia and Malaysia in 1980 and 2002, including population size, sex distribution, birth rates, growth rates and the share aged over 65.',
'Overall, both populations grew, but Malaysia increased faster and became the larger country. Australia had a much higher proportion of older people, while Malaysia recorded higher birth and annual population growth rates in both years.',
'Australia’s population rose from 14.7 million in 1980 to 19.6 million in 2002. Malaysia grew more strongly, from 13.7 million to 24.3 million. The male share in Australia stayed at 49.9%, with females making up 50.1%. In Malaysia, men accounted for 50.3% initially and 50.6% in 2002, while the female share declined from 49.7% to 49.4%.',
'Birth rates fell in both countries, from 1.5% to 1.3% in Australia and from 3.2% to 2.2% in Malaysia. Annual population growth increased slightly in Australia, from 1.2% to 1.3%, but decreased in Malaysia, from 2.4% to 2.1%. Meanwhile, the share aged over 65 rose from 9.6% to 12.4% in Australia and from 3.7% to 4.3% in Malaysia.',
'Không nhầm birth rate với growth rate. Malaysia vượt dân số; Australia già hơn theo tỷ lệ 65+.',
'Body 1: quy mô và giới tính. Body 2: birth/growth/65+.',['intro','overview-trend','compare','from-to'],{'years':[1980,2002],'Australia':{'population_million':[14.7,19.6],'male':[49.9,49.9],'female':[50.1,50.1],'birth_rate':[1.5,1.3],'growth':[1.2,1.3],'over65':[9.6,12.4]},'Malaysia':{'population_million':[13.7,24.3],'male':[50.3,50.6],'female':[49.7,49.4],'birth_rate':[3.2,2.2],'growth':[2.4,2.1],'over65':[3.7,4.3]}})
add(87,
'The pie charts compare the main reasons why students chose a particular UK university in 1987 and 2007.',
'Overall, suitable degree courses were the most common reason in both years. Being close to the parental home became more important, while the shares choosing the university for teaching quality or sports and social activities declined.',
'In 1987, 35% of students selected the university because it offered suitable degree courses. This was followed by the quality of resources at 21% and good sports and social activities at 19%. Teaching quality accounted for 15%, while proximity to the parental home was the least common reason, at 10%. No single reason represented more than half of the responses.',
'By 2007, the share choosing suitable courses had risen slightly to 37%. The proportion wanting to be close to the parental home more than doubled to 22%, becoming the second largest category. In contrast, the figure for resources fell to 17%, while teaching quality dropped to 8%. Sports and social activities experienced the largest decrease, from 19% to just 6%, leaving this as the smallest category in the later year.',
'Suitable courses đứng đầu dưới50%, không majority. Close home10→22 hơn gấp đôi; sports19→6 giảm lớn nhất.',
'Body 1: 1987. Body 2: 2007 với thay đổi chính.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','compare'],{'years':[1987,2007],'resources':[21,17],'courses':[35,37],'close_home':[10,22],'teaching':[15,8],'sports_social':[19,6]})
hold(88,'Trục tung không ghi đơn vị số thuê bao; không tự lấy million từ PDF vì cần xác nhận bản ảnh. Cần bổ sung đơn vị để viết bài định lượng.')
