add(90,
'The table compares the number of cars manufactured in Argentina, Australia and Thailand in 2003, 2005 and 2009.',
'Overall, there was an increase in car production in Argentina and Thailand over the period, while a decline was seen in Australia. In addition, Thailand consistently had the highest figures, despite a fall after its peak in 2005.',
'In 2003, Thailand produced 735,852 cars, well ahead of Australia at 452,163 and Argentina at 235,088. By 2005, the Thai figure had risen sharply to 1,162,356. Argentina also increased its output, reaching 352,759 cars. In contrast, production in Australia fell to 341,268, which meant that Argentina moved slightly ahead of it at the middle point of the table.',
'Between 2005 and 2009, the number of cars made in Argentina continued to grow, ending at 466,089. This was almost double its initial figure. Thailand’s output decreased to 999,963, although it remained higher than in 2003 and exceeded the combined output of the other two countries. Australia experienced another fall, to 245,624 cars, and therefore finished with the lowest production figure among the three.',
'Bản q090 ghi năm giữa 2005, khác q014 là 2006. Bài này giữ nguyên nhãn ảnh; không dùng chung câu chỉ năm.',
'Body 1: 2003–2005. Body 2: 2005–2009.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','similar'],{'years':[2003,2005,2009],'unit':'cars','Argentina':[235088,352759,466089],'Australia':[452163,341268,245624],'Thailand':[735852,1162356,999963]},'Cùng các số với q014 nhưng năm giữa khác. Mẫu mô tả đúng bản ảnh này, chưa khẳng định bản nào là đề gốc.')
add(91,
'The table compares visitor numbers at six World Heritage sites in Australia in 1996, 1998 and 2000.',
'Overall, the Great Barrier Reef attracted by far the most visitors and showed the largest increase. Macquarie Island remained the least visited site. Most sites gained visitors overall, but the rainforest reserve and Macquarie Island ended below their initial figures.',
'The Great Barrier Reef received 1.67 million visitors in 1996. This rose sharply to 2.95 million in 1998 and 3.2 million in 2000. In contrast, visits to the Central Eastern Rainforest Reserve fell gradually from 810,000 to 790,000 and then 770,000. Despite this decline, the reserve remained the second most visited site in all three years.',
'The Blue Mountains increased from 526,000 visitors in 1996 to 581,000 in 2000, while Tasmania Wilderness rose from 450,000 to 483,000. Shark Bay fluctuated, climbing from 84,000 to 102,000 before falling to 89,000. Macquarie Island had much smaller numbers: 350 visitors initially, followed by 310 in 1998 and a partial recovery to 330 in 2000.',
'Macquarie chỉ hàng trăm lượt, không tự thêm nghìn. Great Barrier Reef tăng mạnh và lớn nhất.',
'Body 1: hai site lớn nhất. Body 2: bốn site còn lại.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','sequence'],{'years':[1996,1998,2000],'Great Barrier Reef':[1670000,2950000,3200000],'Central Eastern Rainforest Reserve':[810000,790000,770000],'Blue Mountains':[526000,565000,581000],'Tasmania Wilderness':[450000,475000,483000],'Shark Bay':[84000,102000,89000],'Macquarie Island':[350,310,330]})
hold(92,'Bảng total expenditure không khớp tổng các khoản trong bar (ví dụ A:220+358+430=1008, bảng875); chưa rõ cùng kỳ hay khác mẫu số. Cần xác nhận trước khi viết full bài kết hợp.')
hold(93,'Biểu đồ việc làm thiếu đơn vị (tỷ lệ hay số lượng), trong khi graph phía trên là số graduates. Cần xác nhận đơn vị biểu đồ dưới để không mô tả nhầm.')
add(94,
'The tables compare average working hours for men and women in full-time and part-time jobs in Greece, the Netherlands and the UK in 2002, alongside European averages.',
'Overall, full-time workers had longer hours than part-time workers. Greece recorded the highest figures among the three countries for both types of employment, while the European averages for part-time work were higher than all the national figures shown.',
'For full-time work, Greek women averaged 39.9 hours and men 42.5 hours, both above the European averages of 39.2 and 40.4 hours respectively. In the Netherlands, the two sexes worked the same average of 38 hours. The UK had slightly lower figures, at 37 hours for women and 37.5 for men, making it the lowest of the three countries.',
'Part-time hours were more similar across countries. Greek women worked 29.3 hours on average, compared with 30 for men. In the Netherlands, women worked slightly longer than men, at 29.2 and 28.3 hours respectively. The UK figures were 28 hours for women and 29 for men. All these averages were below the European figures of 34 hours for women and 32 for men.',
'Đơn vị hours; ảnh không nói per week nên mẫu không tự thêm. Netherlands part-time women cao hơn men, full-time bằng nhau.',
'Body 1: full-time. Body 2: part-time.',['intro','static-overview','compare','respectively'],{'unit':'hours (period not specified)','fulltime':{'Greece':[39.9,42.5],'Netherlands':[38,38],'UK':[37,37.5],'Europe':[39.2,40.4]},'parttime':{'Greece':[29.3,30],'Netherlands':[29.2,28.3],'UK':[28,29],'Europe':[34,32]},'order':['women','men']})
add(95,
'The charts show UK undergraduate numbers and government spending per student from 1991 to 2001, as well as students’ family income backgrounds in 1991.',
'Overall, student numbers increased, while government spending per student declined. In 1991, most students came from middle-income families, and those from low-income households formed a much smaller group.',
'The number of university students rose from approximately 1.1 million in 1991 to 1.5 million in 1993. It then increased more gradually to around 1.6 million in 1995 and 1.7 million in 1997. Numbers reached just over 2 million in 1999, before falling slightly to about 2 million in 2001. Over the same period, government spending per student dropped from roughly £6,600 to around £4,800, with most of the fall occurring before the late 1990s.',
'The pie chart shows that 62% of students came from middle-income families in 1991, making this the largest group by a wide margin. A further 30% were from high-income families. Only 8% came from low-income households, less than one third of the high-income share. These background figures refer to 1991 only and do not show how the student population changed later.',
'Cột là khoảng 1.1–2.1 triệu, không phải 110k–210k; pie62/30/8. Không suy ra số sinh viên tăng gây giảm ngân sách.',
'Body 1: number và spending qua thời gian. Body 2: cơ cấu thu nhập 1991.',['intro','overview-trend','from-to','compare'],{'background_1991_percent':{'low':8,'middle':62,'high':30},'students_approx':{'1991':1100000,'1999':2100000,'2001':2000000},'spending_GBP_approx':{'1991':6600,'2001':4800}})
add(96,
'The plans compare the layout of a school library five years ago with its current arrangement.',
'Overall, the library now provides more individual study space and facilities for students’ laptops. Some traditional areas have been replaced by a recording studio and a conference room, while the meeting room and upper bookshelves remain.',
'Five years ago, bookshelves were positioned along both the upper and lower sides of the library. Four studying tables occupied the centre, and a desk for computers stood on the right. On the left were a classroom, a meeting room and a combined borrowing and returning desk. The library office was in the lower-right corner.',
'In the current plan, the central area contains six private studying tables instead of four general tables. The lower bookshelves and the former computer desk have been replaced by desks for students’ laptops. The classroom has become a recording studio, while the meeting room remains in the same position. Borrowing and returning now have separate desks on the lower left. Finally, the former library office has been converted into a conference room, and the bookshelves along the upper wall have been retained.',
'So sánh five years ago/current, không tự đặt năm. Bàn học4→6; office→conference; classroom→recording.',
'Body 1: bố cục cũ. Body 2: thay đổi hiện tại.',['map-overview','map-change','location'])
hold(97,'Hàng Education 1980 có82+17+6=105 và transport54+31+14=99; đơn vị phần trăm cũng không in rõ. Cần xác nhận bản bảng đã sửa, không tự chuẩn hóa.')
hold(98,'Biểu đồ xuất/nhập khẩu không ghi đơn vị trên trục tung (tiền, tỷ lệ hay chỉ số). Cần bổ sung để bài mẫu không tự bịa đơn vị.')
hold(99,'Lời đề ghi1970–2015 nhưng trục kết thúc2000. Cần xác nhận phạm vi trước khi viết mẫu cố định; không tự kéo xu hướng tới2015.')
hold(100,'Biểu đồ waste disposal không có đơn vị trục tung và không có lời đề đầy đủ. Cần xác nhận tonnes/thousands/đơn vị khác trước khi soạn full bài định lượng.')
